@startuml Alarm Setup – Sequence Diagram
title Alarm Setup · Key Sequences

skinparam defaultFontName Roboto
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFCFA
skinparam sequenceArrowColor #37474F
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #2E7D32

actor User
participant "SetupScreen" as UI
participant "SetupViewModel" as VM
participant "IAlarmRepository" as Repo

== Create New Alarm ==

User -> UI : tap FAB (+) from Home
UI -> VM : loadDraft(empty AlarmDraft)

User -> UI : enter title
UI -> VM : updateTitle("Morning Rain")

User -> UI : toggle Readout ON
UI -> VM : setReadout(true)

User -> UI : toggle Ring ON
UI -> VM : setRing(true)

User -> UI : tap "+ Add Condition"
UI -> UI : navigate to CategoryScreen
note right : returns Condition via\nCompose navigation result

UI -> VM : addCondition(selectedCondition)

== Edit Existing Alarm ==

UI -> VM : loadAlarm(alarmId)
activate VM
VM -> Repo : getById(alarmId)
Repo --> VM : Flow<Alarm?>
VM --> UI : StateFlow<AlarmDraft>
deactivate VM

== Modify Condition ==

User -> UI : tap bool-op chip (AND/OR)
UI -> VM : setOperator(index, OR)

User -> UI : tap numerical value badge
UI -> VM : setNumericalValue(index, 70)

== Drag to Reorder Conditions ==

User -> UI : drag condition block
UI -> VM : reorderConditions(from=2, to=0)

== Remove Condition ==

User -> UI : tap × on condition block
UI -> VM : removeCondition(index)

== Save Alarm ==

User -> UI : tap Save
UI -> VM : save()
activate VM
VM -> VM : build Alarm from draft
VM -> Repo : upsert(alarm)
Repo --> VM : alarmId: Long
VM --> UI : navigate back to Home
deactivate VM

== Delete Alarm (Edit Mode) ==

User -> UI : tap red trash icon
UI -> UI : show confirmation dialog
User -> UI : confirm delete
UI -> VM : delete()
VM -> Repo : delete([alarmId])
Repo --> VM : Unit
VM --> UI : navigate back to Home

== Review AI Draft ==

UI -> VM : loadDraft(aiDraft: AlarmDraft)
note right : AI-generated draft pre-fills\nall fields for user review
VM --> UI : StateFlow<AlarmDraft>
User -> UI : review & modify, then tap Save

@enduml
